# Description
  text: On-Site — Santa Ana, CA (this is not a hybrid or remote role)
  text: eJam is a bootstrapped consumer products company that has built, scaled, and exited multiple brands — all without ever taking a dollar of ou
  text: We’re not a startup hoping something works. We’re a team that has done it repeatedly — taken products from zero to eight figures, landed the
  text: This is the place where you’ll see the entire machine — sourcing, product development, packaging, manufacturing, compliance, marketing, mark
  text: We're looking for a Product Development Coordinator to drive new product development across our portfolio. This is a hands-on role at the ce
  text: You'll be the person who takes a product from idea through production-ready — owning the research, vendor coordination, sample management, d
  text: Mandarin (Chinese) fluency is a strong plus, as you will communicate with overseas manufacturers and suppliers in China and our Shanghai off
  text: Research New Product Opportunities
  text: Use tools like Helium 10, Jungle Scout, and similar platforms to identify high-potential SKUs and category opportunities across Amazon, DTC,
  text: Conduct competitive research — pricing, features, positioning, packaging, reviews, and gaps in the market
  text: Compile category analyses and present findings to leadership with clear recommendations
  text: Maintain organized files of benchmarks, specs, market data, and reference materials
  text: Manage the Product Development Pipeline
  text: Own the product pipeline in ClickUp — Kanban boards, project lists, status updates, and timelines across all active SKUs
  text: Track all active development projects and keep deliverables on schedule
  text: Surface blockers early, flag slippage before it becomes a fire, and keep cross-functional teams aligned
  text: Own the accuracy of project documentation — if it’s in the system, it’s correct and current
  text: Coordinate with Manufacturers & Vendors
  text: Communicate directly with manufacturers in China on pricing, samples, specs, timelines, and production issues
  text: Manage the RFQ process: solicit quotes, organize vendor responses, maintain comparison documents
  text: Coordinate sample shipments, evaluate quality, and manage the feedback loop with manufacturers
  text: Track compliance documentation and product testing requirements
  text: Maintain vendor communication logs and track progress across SKUs
  text: Work with the design team on packaging concepts, dielines, and creative assets
  text: Manage the design approval process — route concepts through stakeholders, collect feedback, push to final approval
  text: Coordinate with printers and packaging vendors on specs, proofs, and production timelines
  text: Present to Leadership Weekly
  text: Prepare and deliver a weekly product development presentation to management
  text: Make sure decision-makers have what they need to make calls — not scrambling for data in the room
  text: Cover project status, milestones hit, blockers, timeline changes, and key decisions needed
  text: Distribute meeting notes, action items, and follow-ups — everyone knows what they owe and when
  text: Coordinate with designers, vendors, manufacturers, and internal teams to keep every deliverable on track
  text: Work with external partners on samples, proofs, timelines, and production schedules
  text: Follow up relentlessly — you are the person who makes sure things get done
# Requirements
  text: You have 2–4 years of experience in product development, sourcing, or product coordination in consumer products, CPG, eCommerce, or DTC
  text: You’ve worked with overseas manufacturers — ideally in China — and understand the sourcing and production workflow
  text: You’re experienced with Amazon product research tools (Helium 10, Jungle Scout, or similar)
  text: You’ve used project management tools daily — ClickUp, Asana, Monday.com, or similar
  text: You communicate clearly in writing and in person — no one has to chase you for updates
  text: You’ve coordinated across multiple teams or departments (sourcing, design, marketing, external vendors)
  text: You have high attention to detail — a messy project board or an incorrect spec keeps you up at night
  text: You’re comfortable presenting to leadership and holding the room accountable on timelines
  text: BONUS POINTS (NOT REQUIRED)
  text: Experience with packaging development — dielines, print specs, materials, and vendor coordination
  text: Familiarity with compliance or regulatory documentation (FDA, FTC, EPA, etc.)
  text: Knowledge of PIM systems or product information management
  text: Previous experience at a brand incubator, Amazon aggregator, or multi-brand portfolio company
  text: Experience with retail buyer requirements and retail-ready packaging
  text: Mandarin (Chinese) fluency
  text: THIS ROLE IS NOT FOR YOU IF
  text: You want to own the product roadmap or lead product strategy — this role executes the roadmap, it doesn’t set it
  text: You’re looking for a remote or hybrid position — this is fully on-site in Santa Ana, CA
  text: You’re coming from software product management and expect to write user stories or run sprints — this is physical product development
  text: You’d rather be “thinking big” than managing details — this role IS the details
  text: Full product lifecycle. Real exposure to how CPG products get built.
  text: CEO access. Direct access to the CEO. No layers, no politics. You’ll learn how product decisions get made at the top.
  text: Growth path. As eJam scales, this role scales. Clear path into product development leadership.
  text: $55,000–$72,000 base salary. Range based on experience.
